# =============================================================================
# Limen — example environment configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Nested config uses `__` (env_nested_delimiter).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (PostgreSQL 16 + PostGIS)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local Docker (default for `make up-dev`):
DB__CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://limen:limen@localhost:5432/limen

# Pool sizing
DB__POOL_MIN_SIZE=2
DB__POOL_MAX_SIZE=20

# --- Neon (serverless Postgres) example ---
# Neon does NOT support pg_cron — keep SCHEDULER__CACHE_CLEANUP=apscheduler.
# Use sslmode=require. No code changes needed; only this var changes.
#DB__CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/limen?sslmode=require

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Object store
#   backend = filesystem | s3
#   filesystem is the default for dev/demo.
#   s3 targets any S3-compatible endpoint (MinIO sidecar on the VPS,
#   Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2). Use
#   OBJECT_STORE__ENDPOINT_URL to point at the non-AWS endpoint.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
OBJECT_STORE__BACKEND=filesystem
OBJECT_STORE__ROOT=./object_store_root

# --- MinIO sidecar example (set OBJECT_STORE__BACKEND=s3) ---
#OBJECT_STORE__BUCKET=limen
#OBJECT_STORE__PREFIX=raster/
#OBJECT_STORE__ENDPOINT_URL=http://minio:9000
#OBJECT_STORE__ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
#OBJECT_STORE__SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM provider precedence:
#   1) ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  → Anthropic (Claude API — opzionale, opt-in)
#   2) OPENAI_API_KEY     → OpenAI
#   3) FOUNDRY_*          → Microsoft Foundry
#   4) (fallback)         → llama.cpp (LLM__LLAMACPP_BASE_URL)
# Una chiave cloud vince sempre sul motore locale, a meno che LLM__PROVIDER non
# forzi la scelta. Impostare ANTHROPIC_API_KEY *e' gia'* la configurazione che
# seleziona Claude: non serve altro.
#
# ATTENZIONE — il fallback e' cambiato: prima era Ollama, ora e' llama.cpp.
# Un deploy che si affidava al fallback implicito (il VPS Aruba, che imposta
# solo LLM__OLLAMA_BASE_URL) deve ora dichiarare LLM__PROVIDER=ollama.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#LLM__PROVIDER=              # anthropic | openai | foundry | ollama | llamacpp
#
# Mappa ruolo -> modello. I valori qui sotto sono id Claude: sono i default
# del codice, validi solo per Anthropic/OpenAI/Foundry. I motori locali
# (llamacpp, ollama) onorano SOLO i ruoli dichiarati esplicitamente in
# environment: un ruolo non dichiarato ripiega su LLM__LLAMACPP_MODEL /
# LLM__OLLAMA_MODEL. Senza questo filtro il gateway riceverebbe
# "claude-haiku-4-5" e risponderebbe 400.
#
# Ruoli esistenti nel codice (limen.agents.llm_factory.resolver._ROLE_FIELDS).
# Solo RISK_ANALYST e BRIEFING hanno un executor: gli altri tre sono
# configurazione dichiarata senza call site.
#LLM__MODELS__RISK_ANALYST=claude-haiku-4-5   # JSON stretto -> 'extract' sul gateway
#LLM__MODELS__BRIEFING=claude-sonnet-4-6      # prosa IT 150-250 parole -> 'chat'
#LLM__MODELS__ORCHESTRATOR=claude-opus-4-7    # non usato oggi -> 'fast'
#LLM__MODELS__SCORER=claude-sonnet-4-6        # non usato oggi -> 'fast'
#LLM__MODELS__SUMMARIZER=claude-haiku-4-5     # non usato oggi -> 'fast'
#
# VINCOLO NON NEGOZIABILE: mai 'quality-local' ne' 'glm52' su questi ruoli.
# Sono tutti su percorsi sincroni (richiesta HTTP, tool MCP, tick dello
# scheduler piu' breve della risposta) e questi due modelli generano in
# decine di minuti: il chiamante andrebbe in timeout sul fallback
# deterministico e lo sweep oraria si bloccherebbe in silenzio. Il processo
# rifiuta di partire se ci provi (limen.config.settings.SLOW_GENERATION_MODELS).

# Backend intercambiabili — sceglierne UNO:
#
# 1) llama.cpp / llama-swap (DEFAULT: server di inferenza self-hosted sulla Z8).
#    Nessuna chiave. llama-swap sta davanti a llama-server ed espone la forma
#    OpenAI su /v1/chat/completions, caricando il modello richiesto su richiesta.
#    LLM__LLAMACPP_MODEL e' un id logico (chiave del config.yaml di llama-swap),
#    non un nome di file. Dai container di `make up` usare host.docker.internal.
#    Puntare al GATEWAY LiteLLM, non a llama-swap: routing per nome modello,
#    tetto di spesa e fallback locale->cloud vivono la', e una porta diretta li
#    aggira. Senza suffisso /v1: il client accoda /v1/chat/completions da se'.
#    Dai container di `make up` serve host.docker.internal (l'override
#    API_LLM_LLAMACPP_BASE_URL nel compose lo fa da solo).
LLM__LLAMACPP_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8091
#    Modelli esposti dal gateway (GET /v1/models): fast, chat, extract, embed,
#    quality-local, quality-cloud, glm52. Ripiego per i ruoli non dichiarati
#    in LLM__MODELS__*: chat = 8B per la prosa italiana.
#LLM__LLAMACPP_MODEL=chat
#LLM__LLAMACPP_API_KEY=              # solo se il gateway gira con una chiave
#    Tetto per i ruoli senza override. Dimensionato sui modelli residenti in
#    GPU dietro il gateway, con i GGUF su NVMe striped (uno swap sono secondi,
#    non i ~2 minuti del disco rotante per cui valeva il vecchio 600).
#    Un tetto troppo alto danneggia quanto uno troppo basso, al contrario:
#    quando scade, il chiamante ripiega comunque sul percorso deterministico,
#    quindi l'attesa in piu' serve solo a farti accorgere piu' tardi che il
#    motore e' rotto.
#LLM__LLAMACPP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
#    Tetto per-ruolo, JSON con le etichette dei ruoli come chiavi. Serve solo
#    a un ruolo puntato deliberatamente su un modello lento — cosa che oggi
#    nessun ruolo puo' essere (vedi il vincolo su LLM__MODELS__* sopra).
#LLM__LLAMACPP_ROLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS={"Briefing": 5400}
#
#    Il resolver da' precedenza a una chiave cloud se presente, quindi per
#    restare sul motore locale il provider va dichiarato esplicitamente.
#LLM__PROVIDER=llamacpp
#
# 2) Host Ollama: nessuna chiave, ma ora va dichiarato esplicitamente.
#LLM__PROVIDER=ollama
#LLM__OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
#LLM__OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.6:latest
#
# 3) Ollama Cloud (https://ollama.com): base_url + bearer key, provider forzato.
#LLM__PROVIDER=ollama
#LLM__OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com
#LLM__OLLAMA_API_KEY=
#
# 4) Claude API: basta la chiave (autorilevata, vince sul motore locale).
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT=
#FOUNDRY_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduler
#   cache_cleanup = pg_cron | apscheduler
#   Use `apscheduler` on Neon (pg_cron unavailable).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Pericoli valutati (Fase 1 di #57)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Quali hazard il codice valuta. Il database ha la sua copia nella tabella
# `hazards`, perché mv_latest_risk la incrocia e una vista non può leggere i
# Settings: all'avvio l'API confronta le due e logga `hazards.config_drift`
# se divergono, senza rifiutare la partenza. Le soglie di ogni pericolo
# stanno in src/limen/config/hazards/<hazard>.yaml.
#HAZARDS__ENABLED=["landslide"]

SCHEDULER__CACHE_CLEANUP=apscheduler
SCHEDULER__CACHE_CLEANUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=300
# Manutenzione partizioni giornaliere + retention delle tabelle calde
# (risk_assessments, model_runs). Registrato SEMPRE, indipendentemente da
# SCHEDULER__CACHE_CLEANUP: senza partizioni ogni scrittura finisce nella
# partizione DEFAULT, dove la retention non arriva.
#SCHEDULER__PARTITIONS_INTERVAL_HOURS=6

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logging
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
LOG_JSON=false

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notifications (Phase 7) — Strategy pattern: list channels in
# NOTIFICATIONS__ENABLED_CHANNELS. Channels whose creds are missing
# degrade to a no-op (logged), they DON'T error. Multiple at once OK.
# Format must be a JSON array, e.g. '["telegram","mqtt"]'.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#NOTIFICATIONS__ENABLED_CHANNELS=["telegram","mqtt","email"]

# --- Telegram ---
#NOTIFICATIONS__TELEGRAM__BOT_TOKEN=
#NOTIFICATIONS__TELEGRAM__CHAT_ID=
#NOTIFICATIONS__TELEGRAM__PARSE_MODE=HTML

# --- MQTT (V1 demo uses Mosquitto in docker-compose.demo.yml) ---
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__BROKER_HOST=localhost
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__BROKER_PORT=1883
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__TOPIC=limen/alerts
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__USERNAME=
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__PASSWORD=
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__TLS=false
#NOTIFICATIONS__MQTT__QOS=1

# --- Email (SMTP) ---
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__SMTP_PORT=587
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__USERNAME=
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__PASSWORD=
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__FROM_ADDRESS=alerts@limen.example
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__RECIPIENTS=["ops@example.com"]
#NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__USE_STARTTLS=true

# --- Webhook (agent gateway, e.g. OpenClaw /hooks) ---
# POSTs {text, message, payload} with an optional bearer token — `text` /
# `message` are what OpenClaw /hooks/wake and /hooks/agent require.
# Full guide + setup script: docs/openclaw.md , scripts/setup_openclaw.sh
# OpenClaw on the same host (from the api CONTAINER use host.docker.internal):
#   http://host.docker.internal:18789/hooks/wake
# Remote VPS: https://openclaw.example.com/hooks/wake  (TLS!)
#NOTIFICATIONS__WEBHOOK__URL=
#NOTIFICATIONS__WEBHOOK__TOKEN=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# limen-ops MCP server (agent gateways: OpenClaw & co.)
#   compose service `mcp` serves HTTP on :8766, bound to 127.0.0.1 by
#   default. LIMEN_MCP_BIND=0.0.0.0 exposes it to other machines — do it
#   only behind TLS/reverse-proxy. MCP_ADMIN_TOKEN unset = the admin tools
#   (run_monitor, build_report, forecast_history) are disabled (fail-closed).
# OpenClaw hookup (same host):
#   openclaw mcp set limen-ops '{"url":"http://127.0.0.1:8766/mcp","transport":"streamable-http"}'
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#MCP_ADMIN_TOKEN=
#LIMEN_MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- A2A (Agent2Agent) interop ---
#   Read-only JSON-RPC surface mounted on the API: agent card at
#   /.well-known/agent-card.json, endpoint /a2a (message/send, message/stream,
#   tasks/*). The card's absolute URL is derived from the request; set
#   A2A_PUBLIC_URL when the API sits behind a reverse proxy / different origin.
#A2A_PUBLIC_URL=https://limen.example.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth su database (sostituisce Clerk — PA-compliant, self-hosted). Issue #49.
#   AUTH__ENABLED=false ⇒ endpoint protetti aperti (mappa pubblica + dev/test).
#   Attivandolo, gli endpoint protetti richiedono una sessione valida (cookie
#   httpOnly). I codici di verifica email riusano la config SMTP del canale
#   `email` (NOTIFICATIONS__EMAIL__*). In dev senza SMTP il codice finisce nei log.
#   cookie_secure=true richiede HTTPS — metti false solo per http locale.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#AUTH__ENABLED=false
#AUTH__REGISTRATION_OPEN=true
#AUTH__SESSION_TTL_HOURS=168
#AUTH__COOKIE_SECURE=true
#AUTH__COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax
#AUTH__CODE_TTL_MINUTES=15
#AUTH__CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# Bootstrap del primo admin (idempotente): `limen create-admin`
#LIMEN_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.it
#LIMEN_ADMIN_PASSWORD=cambia-questa-password
#LIMEN_ADMIN_FIRST=Admin
#LIMEN_ADMIN_LAST=Limen

# --- SPID / CIE via OIDC (seam — fase D, issue #49) ---
#   Disattivo finché il client OIDC non è configurato (fail-closed: endpoint 404,
#   bottone "Entra con SPID" disabilitato). SPID vero richiede un Service Provider
#   accreditato AgID + un proxy/aggregatore SPID/CIE OIDC: punta questi endpoint
#   a quel proxy. Il bottone diventa attivo quando SPID__* è impostato.
#SPID__CLIENT_ID=
#SPID__CLIENT_SECRET=
#SPID__ISSUER=https://spid-proxy.example
#SPID__AUTHORIZATION_ENDPOINT=https://spid-proxy.example/oidc/authorize
#SPID__TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://spid-proxy.example/oidc/token
#SPID__USERINFO_ENDPOINT=https://spid-proxy.example/oidc/userinfo
#SPID__REDIRECT_URI=https://limen.example/api/auth/spid/callback
#SPID__POST_LOGIN_URL=https://limen.example/#/dashboard

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Event-driven predictive pipeline — scheduled forecast sweep.
#   Every INTERVAL_HOURS the APScheduler job re-scores each AOI at
#   now+HORIZON_HOURS with Open-Meteo forecast rain; cells at/above
#   MIN_LEVEL trigger a predictive alert on the SAME notification
#   channels (webhook/OpenClaw, Telegram, …), clearly labelled
#   "PREVISIONE" and deduplicated per (AOI, horizon) — never per cell,
#   so forecast alerts can't mask operational ones. Deterministic
#   summary, no LLM. On-demand equivalent: `limen forecast`.
#   ON by default — set FORECAST__ENABLED=false to opt out.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#FORECAST__ENABLED=false
#FORECAST__HORIZON_HOURS=48
#FORECAST__INTERVAL_HOURS=6
#FORECAST__MIN_LEVEL=High
#FORECAST__DEDUP_WINDOW_HOURS=24

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DPC radar nowcast trigger — short-horizon event-driven monitoring.
#   Every INTERVAL_MINUTES the job reads the latest SRI frame (national
#   1 km rain intensity, 5-min refresh, CC-BY-SA) from the DPC radar
#   platform. AOIs with >= MIN_PIXELS km2 at/above MIN_INTENSITY_MMH get
#   their monitoring workflow run immediately (normal alert path);
#   COOLDOWN skips freshly-assessed AOIs. ON by default.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#NOWCAST__ENABLED=true
#NOWCAST__INTERVAL_MINUTES=15
#NOWCAST__MIN_INTENSITY_MMH=30
#NOWCAST__MIN_PIXELS=3
#NOWCAST__COOLDOWN_MINUTES=45

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NASA FIRMS active-fire hotspots (VIIRS 375 m / MODIS 1 km, NRT ~3 h).
#   Fail-closed: without FIRMS__MAP_KEY the feed is inert and the job is
#   not scheduled. The key is free (FIRMS registration) — get one at
#   https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
#   Detections drive two things: an event-driven monitoring run for the
#   AOIs that are burning, and a timely `months_since_fire` for the
#   post-fire F component (days earlier than the EFFIS perimeter).
#   MIN_HOTSPOTS guards against single false positives (industrial
#   flares, sun glint): one pixel is never an event.
#   One national bbox = 1 transaction per source, against a quota of
#   5000 / 10 min, so the default interval is set by NRT latency, not cost.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#FIRMS__MAP_KEY=
#FIRMS__ENABLED=true
#FIRMS__INTERVAL_MINUTES=45
#FIRMS__SOURCES=["VIIRS_SNPP_NRT","VIIRS_NOAA20_NRT","VIIRS_NOAA21_NRT"]
#FIRMS__DAY_RANGE=1
#FIRMS__MIN_CONFIDENCE=nominal
#FIRMS__MIN_CONFIDENCE_PCT=50
#FIRMS__MIN_FRP_MW=0
#FIRMS__MIN_HOTSPOTS=2
#FIRMS__TRIGGER_WINDOW_HOURS=24
#FIRMS__COOLDOWN_MINUTES=90
#FIRMS__BBOX=[6.0,35.0,19.0,48.0]

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Daily national report — deterministic morning briefing (per-region
# summary, national top cells, ML shadow top, 24h alert counts) sent on
# the notification channels at REPORT__HOUR_UTC. Also available on demand
# as the `tool_national_report` MCP tool. ON by default.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#REPORT__ENABLED=true
#REPORT__HOUR_UTC=6

# --- Report HTML statico (job limen-html-report) ---
# Static HTML risk report: zone cards with an interactive Leaflet mini-map each
# (zoom/pan on an OSM/Carto basemap + cell GeoJSON + geographic coordinates),
# rebuilt on the hourly_monitoring cadence and optionally at startup. Written
# under REPORT__HTML_OUTPUT_DIR; older builds pruned per REPORT__HTML_ARCHIVE_KEEP.
REPORT__HTML_ENABLED=true
REPORT__HTML_INTERVAL_HOURS=1        # refresh cadence; 1 = follows hourly_monitoring
REPORT__HTML_RUN_AT_STARTUP=true     # also generate one report at app startup
REPORT__HTML_OUTPUT_DIR=site         # output dir (distinct from reports/ = calibrate/backtest md)
REPORT__HTML_MAX_CLUSTERS=50         # cap on zone cards per build
REPORT__HTML_MIN_LEVEL=High          # alert threshold; falls back lower if no zone crosses it
REPORT__HTML_CLUSTER_EPS_DEG=0.02    # DBSCAN neighbour distance (degrees) for contiguous cells
REPORT__HTML_ARCHIVE_KEEP=240        # HTML builds kept; manifests are kept forever
# Basemap tiles used by the interactive maps (client-side):
#REPORT__HTML_BASEMAP_URL_TEMPLATE=https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/light_all/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
#REPORT__HTML_BASEMAP_ATTRIBUTION=© OpenStreetMap contributors © CARTO
REPORT__HTML_PUBLISH=false           # push the report/ dir to a gh-pages branch (VPS-side)

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ML drift monitoring (B1) — daily PSI/KS on one canonical model feature,
# training vs the live vectors the shadow persists in model_runs
# (breakdown.features — identical keys and scales by construction).
# Informational: the retrain trigger only logs; promotion stays manual.
# Note: with a case-control training set vs full-grid scoring, PSI on a
# weather feature alarms whenever live weather differs from event-time
# weather — read it as regime info, not as an automatic mandate.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#MONITORING__ENABLE_DRIFT_MONITORING=true
#MONITORING__DRIFT_FEATURE=rain.rain_72h_mm
#MONITORING__DRIFT_CHECK_HOURS=24
# Shadow writes ~1M rows/day nationally (~1 GB/day): the cleanup job
# purges model_runs older than this. 0 = keep everything.
#SCORING__MODEL_RUNS_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# --- Dispatch rules ---
ALERT__MIN_LEVEL=Moderate         # Low | Moderate | High | VeryHigh
ALERT__MIN_STATIC_S=0.5           # below-High cells alert only if S >= this (susceptible slope)
ALERT__DEDUP_WINDOW_MINUTES=180   # suppress a repeat alert for the same cell
ALERT__TOP_K=5                    # cells highlighted in the payload
ALERT__MAP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# =============================================================================
# GeoServer vector-data layer (opt-in — mcp-geo-server integration)
#
# Activated only by the `geoserver` compose profile:
#   docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.geoserver.yml \
#     --profile geoserver up -d      (or `make geoserver-up`)
#
# A dedicated Postgres+PostGIS holds the vector layers; GeoServer serves
# them as OGC WMS/WFS. The application images are pulled pre-built from
# GHCR. Endpoints (host ports remapped to coexist with the Limen stack):
#   GeoServer  -> http://localhost:8081/geoserver  (admin/geoserver)
#   Web UI     -> http://localhost:8000
#   MCP agent  -> http://localhost:9000/mcp
#   PostGIS    -> localhost:55433 (gis/gis/gis)
# Tutte pubblicate su 127.0.0.1 (vedi la sezione "Bind delle porte" in fondo).
# NB: 8081 e' GeoServer, NON un motore LLM.
# =============================================================================
# GHCR image refs (override to pin a tag or use a locally-built image).
#GEOSERVER_APP_IMAGE=ghcr.io/agent-engineering-studio/mcp-geo-server:latest
#GEOSERVER_BOOTSTRAP_IMAGE=ghcr.io/agent-engineering-studio/mcp-geo-server:bootstrap

# GeoServer admin credentials (change for anything beyond local testing).
#GEOSERVER_ADMIN_USER=admin
#GEOSERVER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=geoserver

# Shapefile source loaded by the one-shot bootstrap. Defaults to the sibling
# mcp-geoserver repo's ./data. Point at a subset (e.g. Puglia+Basilicata) for
# a faster first test.
#GEOSERVER_SHAPEFILE_DIR=../../../mcp-geoserver/data
#GEO_INIT_WORKSPACE=ispra
#GEO_INIT_DATASTORE=ispra_pg
#GEO_INIT_FORCE=false          # true = drop & reload existing tables (destructive)
#GEO_INIT_SHAPE_ENCODING=ISO-8859-1

# LLM per l'agente MCP in linguaggio naturale:
#   openai (default) | ollama | ollama-cloud | anthropic
# I provider `ollama` di mcp-geo-server parlano il protocollo Ollama nativo
# (/api/chat): puntare GEO_OLLAMA_HOST al gateway NON funziona, va usato
# `openai` (client OpenAI-compatibile con base_url esplicito).
#GEO_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# Endpoint del gateway. Qui il suffisso /v1 SERVE (l'SDK OpenAI accoda solo il
# path), a differenza di LLM__LLAMACPP_BASE_URL sopra dove il client di Limen
# accoda /v1/chat/completions da se'. Dai container: host.docker.internal.
#GEO_OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8091/v1
# Nome modello del gateway. `fast` (il 4B) basta per la scelta dei tool e le
# risposte brevi. MAI quality-local/glm52: tool MCP e chat UI sono sincroni.
#GEO_OPENAI_MODEL=fast
# Backend alternativi, inerti se GEO_LLM_PROVIDER non li seleziona.
#GEO_OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434
#OLLAMA_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5
# Destructive GeoServer tools (delete/WFS-T) are blocked unless true.
#GEO_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE=false

# --- GeoServer as the authoritative source of ISPRA static data ---
# When set, `limen geoserver-sync` (and `limen bootstrap-static`) load the
# IFFI landslide inventory + PAI hazard mosaic from the GeoServer PostGIS
# into the operational iffi_landslides / pai_hazard tables, replacing the
# IdroGeo WFS ingest. Unset ⇒ loader is a no-op. Host port is 55433.
# Also required (once) by `limen seed-comuni`, which imports the ISTAT comune
# boundaries (com01012023_g) into the operational `comuni` table + tags cells;
# after that nothing queries the GeoServer DB in the hot path.
#GEOSERVER_SOURCE__DB_DSN=postgresql://gis:gis@localhost:55433/gis
#GEOSERVER_SOURCE__SCHEMA_NAME=public

# --- DTM (terrain) → slope/aspect/curvature for the S component ---
# The DTM GeoTIFF lives in the /data folder shared with the GeoServer
# container. A single internally-tiled GeoTIFF (e.g. the national 5 m
# HR-DTM, EPSG:6875, 256×256 blocks) works directly — windowed reads touch
# only the blocks under each cell, so the file size is irrelevant. For MANY
# separate tiles, build a virtual mosaic first (`make dtm-vrt`) instead.
# Local slot: ./data/dem/<slug>/dem.tif — see data/README.md for the
# theme-first layout and how to produce each dataset.
#LIMEN_DEM_RASTER=./data/dem/hrdtm5m/HRDTM5m.tif

# --- CORINE Land Cover 2018 (landuse_code per cell) ---
# Open download (no login): SINAnet ISPRA publishes the CLC2018 Italy
# shapefile; rasterize CODE_18 at 100 m for the majority-class zonal:
#   gdal_rasterize -sql "SELECT CAST(CODE_18 AS INTEGER) AS code, geometry
#     FROM CLC18_IT" -dialect sqlite -a code -tr 100 100 -a_nodata 0 \
#     -ot Int16 -co COMPRESS=DEFLATE -co TILED=YES CLC18_IT.shp clc2018.tif
# Source: https://groupware.sinanet.isprambiente.it/uso-copertura-e-consumo-di-suolo/library/copertura-del-suolo/corine-land-cover
#LIMEN_CORINE_RASTER=../mcp-geoserver/data/clc2018_it/clc2018_it_100m.tif

# --- Carta Geolitologica d'Italia 1:500k (litho_weight per cell) ---
# Open WFS (CC-BY, Geoportale Nazionale PCN/MASE), layer GE.CARTAGEOLITOLOGICA:
#   ogr2ogr -f "ESRI Shapefile" carta_geolitologica.shp \
#     "WFS:http://wms.pcn.minambiente.it/ogc?map=/ms_ogc/wfs/Carta_geolitologica.map" \
#     GE.CARTAGEOLITOLOGICA -t_srs EPSG:4326 -nlt PROMOTE_TO_MULTI
# WFS 1.1 returns lat/lon axis order — verify the Extent is lon 6..19 / lat
# 35..47 and, if swapped, fix once with:
#   ogr2ogr -f "ESRI Shapefile" swapped.shp carta_geolitologica.shp \
#     -dialect sqlite -sql "SELECT SwapCoords(geometry) AS geometry, * FROM carta_geolitologica"
# The lithology labels live in `legenda_li` (matched by LITHO_WEIGHTS substrings).
#LIMEN_GEOLOGICAL_SHAPEFILE=../mcp-geoserver/data/carta_geolitologica/carta_geolitologica.shp
#LIMEN_GEOLOGICAL_FIELD=legenda_li

# --- Rete OSM strade/ferrovie (esposizione viabilità per cella) ---
# © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL. Scarica l'estratto Italia da Geofabrik
# (https://download.geofabrik.de/europe/italy-latest.osm.pbf, ~1.8 GB) e
# pre-estrai le reti con ogr2ogr (driver OSM di GDAL):
#   ogr2ogr -f GPKG osm_roads.gpkg italy-latest.osm.pbf lines \
#     -where "highway IN ('motorway','trunk','primary','secondary')"
#   ogr2ogr -f GPKG osm_rails.gpkg italy-latest.osm.pbf lines \
#     -where "railway = 'rail'"
# `limen bootstrap-static` carica la rete in osm_infrastructure e calcola
# distance_to_road_m / distance_to_rail_m per cella. Non impostate =
# passo saltato, l'esposizione degrada ai flag CORINE 12x.
#LIMEN_OSM_ROADS=./data/osm/osm_roads.gpkg
#LIMEN_OSM_RAILWAYS=./data/osm/osm_rails.gpkg

# --- ITALICA / e-ITALICA dated landslide catalogue (backtest truth set) ---
# The §2.5 backtest replays against dated landslide events (all Italy,
# 1996–2021); IFFI on its own is an undated inventory. `limen ingest-events`
# auto-downloads e-ITALICA v4 from the pinned Zenodo DOI (10.5281/zenodo.
# 14204473, CC-BY-4.0) into LIMEN_DATA_DIR and caches it — no manual step.
# Override only to pin a different version or run fully offline:
#LIMEN_DATA_DIR=./data                 # where downloaded datasets are cached
#LIMEN_ITALICA_CSV=./data/events/italica/ITALICA_v4.csv   # explicit local file (skips download)
#LIMEN_ITALICA_URL=https://zenodo.org/api/records/14204473/files/ITALICA_v4.csv/content
# Backtest antecedent-rainfall product: CERRA (5.5 km regional reanalysis,
# 1985–2021) resolves localized triggering rain far better than ERA5 (~28 km).
# Node grid step in degrees defaults to 0.1° (~11 km) to exploit CERRA.
#LIMEN_BACKTEST_RAIN_MODEL=cerra        # or era5_seamless / blank for ERA5
#LIMEN_BACKTEST_RAIN_NODE_DEG=0.1
# Warning horizon: an alert up to this many hours before the event is a hit
# (antecedent-driven landslides warn days ahead; default 120 h / 5 days).
#LIMEN_BACKTEST_LEAD_MAX_HOURS=120

# --- Live monitoring rainfall grid ---
# The hourly MeteoFetch samples precipitation on a node grid over the AOI
# bbox (forecast API, batched ~100 nodes/call) and each cell gets its
# nearest node's series — one regional centroid misses localized convective
# rain. Grid step in degrees; 0 disables (centroid-only).
#METEO_RAIN_NODE_DEG=0.25

# =============================================================================
# Knowledge-graph grounding (V2.x) — advisory, off by default
# =============================================================================
# When enabled, the BriefingAgent calls the KG sidecar's POST /query for
# (region, mechanism) supporting passages and appends Markdown citations
# to the Italian narrative. KG failures degrade silently; numeric scoring
# outputs are NEVER affected.
KG__ENABLED=false
KG__BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
KG__THREAD_ID=landslide-kb
KG__TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3.0          # hard ceiling — briefing never stalls beyond this
KG__CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=3600       # (region, mechanism) cache lifetime in app_cache
KG__TOP_K=4
#KG__API_TOKEN=                  # optional bearer for the sidecar

# --- Sidecar KG: gira dal SUO repo, non da questo compose ---------------
# Il servizio `knowledge-graph` NON e' definito in docker-compose.demo.yml: lo
# stack KG ha un compose completo nel suo repo (docker-compose.ghcr.yml, con
# neo4j + redis + kg-api + kg-ui + kg-mcp + kg-agents). Duplicarne un pezzo qui
# vorrebbe dire tenere allineate a mano due configurazioni.
#
#   1) nel repo knowledge-graph:  docker compose -f docker-compose.ghcr.yml up -d
#   2) qui:                       KG__ENABLED=true
#                                 API_KG_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8000
#
# Dai container serve host.docker.internal, non 127.0.0.1 (che dentro un
# container e' il container stesso). KG__BASE_URL sopra e' il valore lato host.
#
# Il MOTORE del sidecar si configura nel suo repo, non qui: il suo default e'
# gia' `llamacpp` (client OpenAI su /v1), da puntare allo stesso gateway :8091
# che usa l'API di Limen (KG_LLM_PROVIDER, LLAMACPP_BASE_URL,
# LLAMACPP_EXTRACTION_MODEL, EMBEDDING_PROVIDER, LLAMACPP_EMBEDDING_*).
#
# REDIS_VECTOR_DIM (nel suo repo) NON e' un parametro libero: l'indice
# vettoriale Redis e' dimensionato su quel numero, quindi cambiare modello di
# embedding vuol dire ricostruire l'indice e re-ingestare il corpus. 1024 =
# Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B, il modello dietro `embed` sul gateway — misurato, non
# assunto:
#   curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8091/v1/embeddings \
#     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"model":"embed","input":"x"}' \
#     | python -c 'import sys,json; print(len(json.load(sys.stdin)["data"][0]["embedding"]))'
#
# ATTENZIONE (2026-09-03): kg-api:latest su GHCR e' ancora costruita da eab6c0b
# (11 giugno) perche' la CI di quel repo e' rossa e il publish e' gated su di
# essa: l'immagine pubblicata NON ha il provider llama.cpp/OpenAI, anche se il
# codice e' su main. Vedi knowledge-graph#7 (blocco) e #6 (provider openai).
#API_KG_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8000

# =============================================================================
# Clerk auth — DEPRECATO / RIMOSSO (non ammesso per la PA).
# =============================================================================
# Sostituito dall'auth su database (blocco AUTH__ più sopra + src/limen/auth/,
# issue #49). Il codice di validazione JWT Clerk resta finché non si conclude
# la migrazione, ma è disattivato di default e non usato dal frontend.
CLERK__ENABLED=false

# =============================================================================
# limen-ops MCP server (agent tools over Limen itself)
# =============================================================================
# `limen mcp-serve` exposes risk_summary / top_risk_cells / cell_breakdown /
# recent_alerts (read-only) + run_monitor (admin). Register it in an agent
# gateway (OpenClaw, Claude Desktop, ...) next to ispra-geo and geoserver-mcp.
#LIMEN_MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio        # stdio (default) | http (:8766)
# Admin token for the mutating run_monitor tool. UNSET = tool disabled
# (fail-closed), same pattern as the geodata MCP.
#MCP_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Frontend (Vite) dietro un reverse proxy
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_URL e VITE_TILESERV_URL li risolve il BROWSER, non il container:
# dietro un proxy 'localhost' e' la macchina di chi guarda, non il server.
# Le rotte dell'API nascono tutte sotto /api, quindi basta l'origine nuda.
#VITE_API_URL=https://esempio.it
#VITE_TILESERV_URL=https://esempio.it/tiles
#
# Vite 5.4.12+ rifiuta le richieste con un Host che non riconosce (fix per il
# DNS rebinding): dietro proxy l'Host e' il dominio pubblico, e senza elencarlo
# il dev server risponde "Blocked request. This host is not allowed." a tutto.
#VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=esempio.it

# =============================================================================
# Bind delle porte pubblicate — Docker scavalca ufw
#
# Docker pubblica le porte scrivendo nelle PROPRIE catene iptables, consultate
# *prima* di quelle di ufw: il `default deny incoming` dell'host NON protegge
# una porta pubblicata da un container. Un database o un broker MQTT
# raggiungibili da tutta la rete locale sono un problema concreto.
#
# Ogni servizio ha quindi una variabile di bind con default 127.0.0.1. Le porte
# restano pubblicate (non rimosse) perche' il workflow documentato
# `uv run limen migrate/seed/...` da host ci si collega — vedi
# DB__CONNECTION_STRING e GEOSERVER_SOURCE__DB_DSN sopra.
#
# Per esporre qualcosa al pubblico usa un reverse proxy su 443, NON un bind a
# 0.0.0.0. Se lo alzi comunque, mettici davanti TLS e autenticazione.
# =============================================================================
#LIMEN_PG_BIND=127.0.0.1              # postgres 5432 (demo + dev)
#LIMEN_API_BIND=127.0.0.1             # limen-api 8080
#LIMEN_MQTT_BIND=127.0.0.1            # mosquitto 1883 (anonimo!)
#LIMEN_TILESERV_BIND=127.0.0.1        # pg_tileserv 7800
#LIMEN_FRONTEND_BIND=127.0.0.1        # Vite dev server 5173
#                                     # (nessun LIMEN_KG_BIND: il sidecar KG
#                                     #  gira dal suo repo, vedi sotto)
#LIMEN_MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1             # limen-ops MCP 8766
#LIMEN_GEOSERVER_BIND=127.0.0.1       # GeoServer 8081
#LIMEN_GEOSERVER_WEBUI_BIND=127.0.0.1 # chat+map web UI 8000
#LIMEN_GEOSERVER_MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1   # geoserver-mcp 9000
#LIMEN_GEOSERVER_PG_BIND=127.0.0.1    # PostGIS vettoriale 55433
#LIMEN_GEODATA_PG_BIND=127.0.0.1      # geodata-db 55432
#LIMEN_GEODATA_MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1     # ispra-geo MCP 8765
